The note pinger fires once at the due minute; if that ping was missed the
note was never mentioned again. Deadline Watch (src/deadline_watch.py)
classifies open notes with a due date as overdue (still open, last 30 days;
recurring notes excluded, older backlog summarized) or due soon.

- New scheduled task "Deadline Watch" (check_deadlines, 08:41 + 17:41):
  notifies once per note/state/due date, silent when nothing is new.
- Daily brief gains a "Deadlines" section (overdue + next 48h).
- Owner-scoped loader (null-owner notes only on single-user installs),
  titles cleaned/capped; stdlib-only module with injectable notes/clock/state.
- tests/test_deadline_watch.py (12 tests), docs/deadlines.md, ROADMAP.

